not pixel art, it's all math art / vector art drawn to canvas. the model outputs coordinates and colors instead of placing pixels e.g.

    for (const [pu, pv] of [[u0, v0], [u1, v0], [u0, v1], [u1, v1]]) campPost(ctx, at, pu, pv, EAVE);
    campPoly(ctx, [at(u0, v0, EAVE), at(u0, v1, EAVE), at(um, v1, RIDGE), at(um, v0, RIDGE)], THATCH, 0.9);
    campThatch(ctx, at(u0, v0, EAVE), at(um, v0, RIDGE), at(um, v1, RIDGE), at(u0, v1, EAVE));

that's four posts and a roof slope. it allows for some weird things like tweening animation vs frames / spritesheets.
